016.  The transmission pump may seize causing a loss of hydraulic pressure.","consequence":"If the transmission loses hydraulic pressure, the vehicle may lose motive power, increasing the risk of a crash.","remedy":"Chrysler will notify owners, and dealers will replace the transmission pump, free of charge.  The recall began on August 18, 2016.  Owners may contact Chrysler customer service at 1-800-853-1403.  Chrysler's number for this recall is S44.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":26298,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=16V461000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":6,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2015","make":"DODGE","model":"GRAND CARAVAN"},{"year":"2015","make":"CHRYSLER","model":"TOWN AND COUNTRY"},{"year":"2016","make":"DODGE","model":"GRAND CARAVAN"},{"year":"2016","make":"RAM","model":"PROMASTER"},{"year":"2016","make":"DODGE","model":"JOURNEY"},{"year":"2016","make":"CHRYSLER","model":"TOWN AND COUNTRY"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"16V044000","received":"2016-01-28","manufacturer":"Chrysler (FCA US LLC)","component":"VISIBILITY:WINDSHIELD","summary":"FCA US LLC (Chrysler) is recalling certain model year 2015-2016 Chrysler Town and Country, and 2014-2015 Dodge Grand Caravan vehicles manufactured August 16, 2014, to December 5, 2015.  The windshield on the affected vehicles may have been installed using expired urethane primer, allowing the windshield to become displaced in the event of a crash.  As such, these vehicles fail to comply with the requirements of Federal Motor Vehicle Safety Standard (FMVSS) number 212, \"Windshield Mounting.\"","consequence":"If the windshield dislodges during a crash, there is an increased risk of occupant injury.","remedy":"Chrysler will notify owners, and dealers will replace the windshield, free of charge.  The recall began March 4, 2016. Owners may contact Chrysler customer service at 1-800-853-1403.  Chrysler's number for this recall is S02.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":184,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=16V044000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":4,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2014","make":"DODGE","model":"GRAND CARAVAN"},{"year":"2015","make":"DODGE","model":"GRAND CARAVAN"},{"year":"2015","make":"CHRYSLER","model":"TOWN AND COUNTRY"},{"year":"2016","make":"CHRYSLER","model":"TOWN AND COUNTRY"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"25V876000","received":"2025-12-18","manufacturer":"Rollx Vans","component":"EQUIPMENT ADAPTIVE/MOBILITY:WHEELCHAIR RESTRAINTS/SECUREMENT:LATCH/ANCHOR:","summary":"Rollx Vans (Rollx) is recalling certain GMC Yukon, Sierra, Chevrolet Express 2500, Ford Transit, E-250, Toyota Sienna, Sienna Hybrid, Honda Odyssey, Chrysler Town and Country, Voyager, Pacifica, Dodge Grand Caravan, and Ram Promaster vehicles equipped with QRT-Deluxe and QRT-Max wheelchair restraints. Please refer to Rollx's recall report for specific model year information. The retractors may not lock, preventing the wheelchair from being properly secured.","consequence":"An unsecured wheelchair can move during transit, increasing the risk of injury.","remedy":"Rollx will work with Q'Straint to inspect and replace the retractors as necessary, free of charge. Owner notification letters were mailed February 5, 2026. Owners may contact Rollx's customer service at 1-800-956-6668.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":86,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=25V876000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":52,"campaign_v